    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter tonight\u2019s slate with a potent offensive profile, anchored by **Yordan Alvarez** (82.97) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.98). **Yordan Alvarez** remains our premier option against Merrill Kelly; with a projected xwOBA of .451 and a favorable SP xERA of 5.23, he is the clear centerpiece of our lineup. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** provides critical upside in our scarcest category\u2014stolen bases\u2014and his matchup against Junk is optimized by his leadoff position and a favorable 15% boost for SP skill, effectively mitigating a slight park disadvantage. **Christian Yelich** (75.84) also grades as an elite play; his high score is bolstered by a 10% wind-out advantage and a favorable matchup against Lowder, whose slower delivery significantly increases the stolen base viability for **Christian Yelich**.\n\nPlatoon advantages and situational mechanics are dictating the remainder of the order. **Lars Nootbaar** (62.86) and **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** (62.08) both benefit from favorable dynamic platoon splits, with **Lars Nootbaar** utilizing an 11% boost against Javier to secure a strong start. While **Trea Turner** (55.25) remains in the lineup, his score is suppressed by a difficult matchup against Sale (2.79 xERA), reinforcing the need for our high-floor outfielders to carry the weight tonight. **Chase Meidroth** (42.95) represents the bottom of our efficiency threshold; he remains active, but his low score reflects the reality of his #8 position and a lack of platoon leverage against Matthews.\n\nRegarding our bench, **Colt Keith** was the closest to cracking the starting lineup, but was ultimately excluded due to the combination of a difficult matchup against L.T. Allen and a lack of confirmed lineup placement. With **Casey Schmitt** confirmed on the IL, our bench depth is currently limited, forcing us to rely on our core starters to maintain efficiency across the 5x5 categories. We will continue to monitor the status of **Jacob Gonzalez**, **Hector Rodriguez**, **Luis Pena**, and **Pedro Ramirez** for potential late-season roster adjustments as we navigate these remaining games. As a final note, managers should remain cautious of the volatility inherent in **Trea Turner**'s matchup against an elite arm, though his category-defining speed keeps him in the daily rotation.",
